    {"name": "CONFIG.TXT", "text": "# Aspen settings. One setting per line: name = value. Anything after # is a comment. Order doesn't matter.\n# Every line is optional. A setting that is left out, or switched off with a # in front, takes its default: the\n# \"Default\" in its comment, or the value on its switched-off line. A value of - also means \"the default\".\n# Mistakes are reported in the log (and the red LED flashes 6 times); the logger runs anyway, using the default for\n# any line it couldn't read. Check a card before a deployment with gemlog's check_aspen_config or the app's Check tab.\n# What each setting does: https://github.com/ajakef/gemlog/blob/main/config_file_aspen.md\n\n# ---- What to record ----\ngains = 128, 128, 128, 128 # channels 1-4: 0 (off), 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, or 128. Default 128, 128, 128, 128\n                          # Listing fewer than 4 turns the rest off, so \"gains = 128\" is infrasound only\nsample_rate = 200         # samples per second: 100, 200, 400, 800, 1000, 2000, or 4000 (channel 1 only). Default 200\n\n# ---- GPS ----\ngps_mode = 1              # 1 or cycled, 2 or on (always on), 3 or off, 4 or adaptive (cycle length auto-adjusted). Default 1\ngps_cycle_minutes = 30    # minutes between GPS wake-ups (modes 1 and 4), 1-255. Default 30\ngps_quota = 20            # PPS pulses the clock collects at each wake-up, 1-255. Default 20\n#gps_settle_s = 20        # seconds after each wake-up before PPS pulses are used, 0-120\n\n# ---- Names written in the miniSEED files ----\n#network = -              # up to 2 letters/digits. - means blank\n#station = -              # up to 5 letters/digits. - means the logger's serial number\n#location = -             # up to 2 letters/digits. - means blank\n#channels = -, -, -, -    # 3 letters/digits each; channel1 ... channel4 set one at a time. - means the default\n                          # for the sample rate: HDF, EHZ, EHN, EHE at 100-200 sps; CDF, DHZ, DHN, DHE at 400-800;\n                          # FDF, GHZ, GHN, GHE at 1000-4000\n\n# ---- Files, serial port, Bluetooth ----\n#file_minutes = 1440      # length of each file in minutes, 1-1440; files start at whole multiples of it (UTC)\n#serial_data = 0          # 1 or on: also send the data lines over the USB serial port (for the plotters)\n#serial_gps = 0           # 1 or on: also send the GPS lines\n#serial_health = 1        # 0 or off: don't send the health (H) lines over the USB serial port\n#health_s = 5             # seconds between health (H) lines, 1-60\n#bluetooth = 1            # 0 or off: radio off; 1 or on: a phone can connect and show the serial lines\n\n# ---- Cell accessory (daily check-in) ----\n#checkin_minutes = 0      # longest daily check-in, 1-30 minutes; 0 means no accessory\n#checkin_hour = 12        # UTC hour of the daily check-in, 0-23\n", "format": "named", "problems": [], "settings": {"gain1": 128, "gain2": 128, "gain3": 128, "gain4": 128, "gps_cycle_minutes": 30, "gps_mode": 1, "gps_quota": 20, "sample_rate": 200}, "messages": []},
    {"name": "CONFIG.TXT", "text": "128 # channel 1 gain\n64 # channel 2 gain\n64 # channel 3 gain\n64 # channel 4 gain\n400 # sample rate (100, 200, 400, 800, 1000, 2000, or 4000 samples per second; 4000: channel 1 only)\n1 # gps_mode (1 cycled, 2 always on, 3 off, 4 cycled, with the cycle adjusted to keep timing errors small)\n30 # gps_cycle_minutes\n20 # gps_quota\n1 # use_compression (no longer affects the card's files, but keep this line so the lines below are read in order)\n- # network code (2 characters at most; - means blank)\n- # station code (5 characters at most; - means the serial number)\n- # location code (2 characters at most; - means blank)\n- # channel 1 code (3 characters; - means HDF at 100-200 sps, CDF at 400-800, FDF at 1000-4000)\n- # channel 2 code (3 characters; - means EHZ at 100-200 sps, DHZ at 400-800, GHZ at 1000-2000)\n- # channel 3 code (3 characters; - means EHN, DHN, or GHN, as for channel 2)\n- # channel 4 code (3 characters; - means EHE, DHE, or GHE, as for channel 2)\n0 # checkin_minutes (cell accessory: longest daily check-in, 1 to 30 minutes; 0 means no accessory)\n12 # checkin_hour (cell accessory: UTC hour of the daily check-in, 0 to 23)\n", "format": "positional"},
